## CONSTRUCT queries

It is also possible to run SPARQL CONSTRUCT queries which can be used to return RDF results.

For example:

<!-- livebook:{"break_markdown":true} -->

First, use the local graph introduced above to see a fully reproducible CONSTRUCT example. `Session.query/2` returns `%{kind: :graph, graph: turtle}`; querying that output checks that both names were constructed.

```elixir
:ok = Session.read_data(rudof, rdf)

{:ok, %{kind: :graph, graph: graph}} =
  Session.query(
    rudof,
    "PREFIX : <http://example.org/>\nCONSTRUCT { ?person :name ?name }\nWHERE { ?person a :Person ; :name ?name }\n"
  )

{:ok, %{rows: names}} =
  Rudof.query(graph, "SELECT ?s ?name WHERE { ?s <http://example.org/name> ?name }")

assert length(names) == 2
IO.puts(graph)
```

This runs the upstream Wikidata CONSTRUCT query against the same endpoint. The returned RDF graph is serialized by the native library; Elixir only displays it.

```elixir
Session.with_session(fn remote ->
  :ok = Session.read_endpoint(remote, wikidata_endpoint)

  query = ~S"""
  PREFIX wd:  <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/>
  PREFIX wdt: <http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/>
  PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
  PREFIX :    <http://example.org/>

  CONSTRUCT {
     ?p a     :Person ;
        :name ?person ;
        :occupation ?occupation
  } WHERE {
      ?p wdt:P31 wd:Q5 ;
         wdt:P106 ?o ;
         rdfs:label ?person ;
         wdt:P19 wd:Q14317 .
    ?o rdfs:label ?occupation
    FILTER (lang(?person) = "en" && lang(?occupation) = "en")
  }
  LIMIT 10
  """

  {:ok, %{kind: :graph, graph: graph}} = Session.query(remote, query)
  IO.puts(graph)
end)
```

## References

### Resources for learning SPARQL

* [Learning SPARQL](https://learningsparql.com/) book and blog by Bob Ducharne.
* [SPARQL tutorial](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:SPARQL_tutorial) from Wikidata

### Lists of SPARQL endpoints

* [SPARQL endpoints](https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Lists/SPARQL_endpoints) collected in Wikidata
* [SPARQL endpoints](https://www.w3.org/wiki/SparqlEndpoints) collected at W3C.

## Close the session

Release the native state when finished. To revisit earlier cells, evaluate from the beginning.

```elixir
:ok = Session.close(rudof)
```
